# Playwright Storagestate

<p>Storage state is a way to save and reuse browser session data (cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage) so you don't repeat actions like login in every test.</p>

## Save Storage state
```
await context.storageState({ path: 'storageState.json' });
```

## Load Storage state into new context

```
const context = await browser.newContext({
  storageState: 'storageState.json'
});
```

## Most Common Use Case — Skip Login in Every Test
## Step 1: Create a global setup to login once

```
// global-setup.ts
import { chromium } from '@playwright/test';

async function globalSetup() {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();

  await page.goto('https://myapp.com/login');
  await page.locator('#email').fill('user@example.com');
  await page.locator('#password').fill('password123');
  await page.locator('#submit').click();
  await page.waitForURL('/dashboard');

  // Save session to file
  await page.context().storageState({ path: 'storageState.json' });
  await browser.close();
}

export default globalSetup;
```
## Step 2: Register it in playwright.config.ts

```
// playwright.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  globalSetup: './global-setup.ts',
  use: {
    storageState: 'storageState.json', // applied to all tests
  }
});
```
## Step 3: Tests start already logged in

```
// tests/dashboard.spec.ts
test('dashboard loads correctly', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard'); // already authenticated!
  await expect(page.locator('.welcome')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Multiple User Roles
A very common real-world pattern — different state files per role.

```
// global-setup.ts
async function globalSetup() {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();

  // Admin user
  const adminPage = await browser.newPage();
  await loginAs(adminPage, 'admin@app.com', 'adminpass');
  await adminPage.context().storageState({ path: '.auth/admin.json' });

  // Regular user
  const userPage = await browser.newPage();
  await loginAs(userPage, 'user@app.com', 'userpass');
  await userPage.context().storageState({ path: '.auth/user.json' });

  await browser.close();
}
```
```
// Use per-test via fixtures
test.use({ storageState: '.auth/admin.json' });

test('admin can delete users', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/admin/users');
  await page.locator('.delete-btn').first().click();
  await expect(page.locator('.success-toast')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Inline Usage (Without a File)
Save and pass state directly as an object — useful for dynamic sessions.

```
const context1 = await browser.newContext();
const page1 = await context1.newPage();
// ... do login ...
const state = await context1.storageState(); // no path = returns object

// Reuse in another context
const context2 = await browser.newContext({ storageState: state });
const page2 = await context2.newPage();
// page2 is now authenticated
```

## Test role-based access control

```
test.describe('Admin only pages', () => {
  test.use({ storageState: '.auth/admin.json' });

  test('admin sees delete button', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/users');
    await expect(page.locator('.delete-btn')).toBeVisible();
  });
});

test.describe('Regular user pages', () => {
  test.use({ storageState: '.auth/user.json' });

  test('user cannot see delete button', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/users');
    await expect(page.locator('.delete-btn')).toBeHidden();
  });
});
```
